  "result": "I'd want to make changing your mind feel safe.\n\nMany of the world's hardest problems, like political fights that never end, families that stop speaking, and institutions that refuse to correct course, persist partly because admitting error feels like losing a part of yourself. If people could say \"I was wrong\" without shame, and treat new evidence as good news rather than a threat, a lot of other problems would get easier to solve. Disagreements would be more about what's true and less about who wins.\n\nI'd be wary of making this too literal, though. A world where everyone is forced to agree would be worse, and some people change their minds for bad reasons. I'd want to make the change feel like freedom, not pressure.\n\nWhat would you change?",
